WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.700 --> 00:00:05.445
Here is a small pipeline for card fees.

2
00:00:05.445 --> 00:00:09.668
Take the numbers one to three, and multiply each one by 100.

3
00:00:10.700 --> 00:00:11.918
The line has run.

4
00:00:11.918 --> 00:00:14.066
Inside map there is a counter.

5
00:00:14.066 --> 00:00:16.501
How many times has map run so far?

6
00:00:18.733 --> 00:00:19.092
Zero.

7
00:00:19.092 --> 00:00:22.032
Building the chain ran none of your code.

8
00:00:22.233 --> 00:00:26.119
Flux.range made an object that knows how to count to three.

9
00:00:26.119 --> 00:00:30.795
map made a second object that wraps the first and stores your function.

10
00:00:30.795 --> 00:00:32.507
That is all assembly does.

11
00:00:32.507 --> 00:00:33.759
It writes a recipe.

12
00:00:33.967 --> 00:00:36.811
Now add a subscriber, and call subscribe.

13
00:00:37.033 --> 00:00:39.024
Which end starts moving first?

14
00:00:41.233 --> 00:00:42.031
The bottom.

15
00:00:42.031 --> 00:00:46.527
The subscriber subscribes to map, and map subscribes to range.

16
00:00:46.527 --> 00:00:48.123
The signal travels up.

17
00:00:48.333 --> 00:00:52.351
Then a request for items travels up the same path, to the source.

18
00:00:52.567 --> 00:00:54.197
Only now does range emit.

19
00:00:54.197 --> 00:00:59.087
Each number flows down through map, which multiplies it, to the subscriber.

20
00:01:00.667 --> 00:01:03.361
Then a completion signal follows them down.

21
00:01:03.967 --> 00:01:06.075
Now call subscribe a second time.

22
00:01:06.075 --> 00:01:08.375
What does the second subscriber get?

23
00:01:10.600 --> 00:01:12.883
The whole run again, from the start.

24
00:01:12.883 --> 00:01:16.053
Range counts again, and map runs three more times.

25
00:01:18.233 --> 00:01:21.429
Each subscriber gets its own run, from the source.

26
00:01:21.429 --> 00:01:23.729
That is what a cold publisher means.

27
00:01:23.933 --> 00:01:29.337
So if the source were a Mono that charges a card, two subscribes would be two charges.

28
00:01:30.367 --> 00:01:33.316
In code, the first statement only builds.

29
00:01:33.316 --> 00:01:35.258
The subscribe line runs it.

30
00:01:35.258 --> 00:01:37.704
Kotlin calls the same Reactor API.

31
00:01:38.533 --> 00:01:39.174
The rule.

32
00:01:39.174 --> 00:01:41.096
Assembly writes the recipe.

33
00:01:41.096 --> 00:01:44.441
Every subscribe runs it again, from the source.

34
00:01:44.667 --> 00:01:45.651
Check yourself.

35
00:01:45.651 --> 00:01:48.079
This chain is subscribed three times.

36
00:01:48.079 --> 00:01:50.639
How many times does map's function run?

37
00:01:53.367 --> 00:01:53.784
Nine.

38
00:01:53.784 --> 00:01:56.708
Three items, in each of three runs.
